<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Complex of Koguryo Tombs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Complex of Goguryeo Tombs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Complex of Koguryo Tombs is a group of more than thirty tombs of the Goguryeo kingdom near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a> and Nampo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>, listed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2004. Many contain wall paintings of daily life, hunting, processions, guardian animals and constellations. The same year <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> listed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capital-cities-and-tombs-of-the-ancient-koguryo-kingdom">Capital Cities and Tombs of the Ancient Koguryo Kingdom</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/complex-of-koguryo-tombs.jpg" alt="Complex of Koguryo Tombs" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sgnpkd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_King_Tongmyong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
